### ============================================================================
### VARIABLES GLOBALES Y ENTORNO
### ============================================================================
@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000/api/v1

### ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 1. HEALTH CHECK (Validar que la API y BD Master están vivas)
### ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{baseUrl}}/health
Accept: application/json


### ============================================================================
### SECCIÓN A: INFRAESTRUCTURA Y SEGURIDAD (MASTER DB)
### ============================================================================

### 2. Crear un Tenant (Aprovisionamiento de BD)
# @name createTenant
POST {{baseUrl}}/tenants
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Club Tenis Elite",
  "slug": "club-tenis-elite-01"
}

### -> Capturamos el Tenant ID
@tenantId = {{createTenant.response.body.id}}

### 3. Listar todos los Tenants (Prueba de Query DTO)
GET {{baseUrl}}/tenants?limit=10&page=1&sortBy=createdAt
Accept: application/json

### 4. Crear el Primer Usuario Administrador en el Tenant
# @name createUser
POST {{baseUrl}}/users
Content-Type: application/json
X-Tenant-Id: {{tenantId}}

{
  "name": "Admin Club Elite",
  "email": "admin@clubelite.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### 5. Iniciar Sesión (Generación de JWT)
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
X-Tenant-Id: {{tenantId}}

{
  "email": "admin@clubelite.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### -> Capturamos el Token JWT (Si tu API devuelve 'token' en vez de 'access_token', cámbialo aquí)
@authToken = {{login.response.body.accessToken}}


### ============================================================================
### SECCIÓN B: OPERACIONES DE NEGOCIO (TENANT DB)
### ============================================================================

### ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
### MÓDULO: CANCHAS (COURTS)
### ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 6. Crear una Cancha
# @name createCourt
POST {{baseUrl}}/courts
Content-Type: application/json
X-Tenant-Id: {{tenantId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

{
  "name": "Cancha Central",
  "sport": "Tennis",
  "pricePerHour": 50.00,
  "status": "AVAILABLE"
}

### -> Capturamos el ID de la cancha
@courtId = {{createCourt.response.body.id}}

### 7. Listar Canchas (Probando filtros: sport=Tennis)
GET {{baseUrl}}/courts?sport=Tennis&sortBy=name
X-Tenant-Id: {{tenantId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### 8. Obtener Cancha por ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/courts/{{courtId}}
X-Tenant-Id: {{tenantId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### 9. Actualizar Cancha (Cambio de precio y estado)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/courts/{{courtId}}
Content-Type: application/json
X-Tenant-Id: {{tenantId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

{
  "pricePerHour": 65.50,
  "status": "MAINTENANCE"
}


### ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
### MÓDULO: CLIENTES (CUSTOMERS)
### ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 10. Crear un Cliente
# @name createCustomer
POST {{baseUrl}}/customers
Content-Type: application/json
X-Tenant-Id: {{tenantId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

{
  "name": "Carlos Alcaraz",
  "email": "carlos@alcaraz.com",
  "phone": "+34600123456"
}

### -> Capturamos el ID del cliente
@customerId = {{createCustomer.response.body.id}}

### 11. Listar Clientes
GET {{baseUrl}}/customers?limit=5
X-Tenant-Id: {{tenantId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### 12. Actualizar Cliente (Añadir un nuevo teléfono)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/customers/{{customerId}}
Content-Type: application/json
X-Tenant-Id: {{tenantId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

{
  "phone": "+34999888777"
}


### ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
### MÓDULO: RESERVAS (RESERVATIONS)
### ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 13. Crear una Reserva (Vinculando Cliente y Cancha)
# @name createReservation
POST {{baseUrl}}/reservations
Content-Type: application/json
X-Tenant-Id: {{tenantId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

{
  "date": "2026-09-01T00:00:00.000Z",
  "startTime": "2026-09-01T10:00:00.000Z",
  "endTime": "2026-09-01T12:00:00.000Z",
  "status": "CONFIRMED",
  "customerId": "{{customerId}}",
  "courtId": "{{courtId}}"
}

### -> Capturamos el ID de la reserva
@reservationId = {{createReservation.response.body.id}}

### 14. Listar Reservas (Filtrando por estado CONFIRMED)
GET {{baseUrl}}/reservations?status=CONFIRMED
X-Tenant-Id: {{tenantId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### 15. Obtener Reserva por ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/reservations/{{reservationId}}
X-Tenant-Id: {{tenantId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### 16. Actualizar Reserva (Cambiar estado a CANCELLED)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/reservations/{{reservationId}}
Content-Type: application/json
X-Tenant-Id: {{tenantId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

{
  "status": "CANCELLED"
}


### ============================================================================
### SECCIÓN C: FLUJO DE ELIMINACIÓN (CLEANUP)
### ============================================================================

### 17. Eliminar la Reserva
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/reservations/{{reservationId}}
X-Tenant-Id: {{tenantId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### 18. Eliminar el Cliente
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/customers/{{customerId}}
X-Tenant-Id: {{tenantId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### 19. Eliminar la Cancha
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/courts/{{courtId}}
X-Tenant-Id: {{tenantId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### 20. Suspender el Tenant (Master DB - Cambio de Estado)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}/status
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "INACTIVE"
}